From: Kali NetHunter rhodep port
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: rhodep: give the camera PMIC its input supply

PM6125's S6 feeds the FAN53870's low LDO group -- LDO1 and LDO2, which
are cam_vdig -- and the vendor device tree says so outright:

	vin1-supply = <&S6A>;

Without it Linux reports `s6 = disabled, users=0` while that rail is
physically powering the camera. Nothing breaks today, but a rail the
kernel believes is free is a rail something may legitimately switch off,
and that failure would arrive much later as a camera that used to work.

--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm6375-motorola-rhodep.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm6375-motorola-rhodep.dts
@@ -516,6 +510,16 @@
 		compatible = "onnn,fan53870";
 		reg = <0x35>;
 		enable-gpios = <&tlmm 33 GPIO_ACTIVE_HIGH>;
+
+		/*
+		 * PM6125's S6 feeds the low LDO group (LDO1/LDO2, i.e.
+		 * cam_vdig), which the vendor device tree spells out as
+		 * vin1-supply = <&S6A>. Without this Linux believes S6 is
+		 * disabled with no users while it is physically powering
+		 * the camera, and a rail nobody claims is a rail something
+		 * may legitimately switch off.
+		 */
+		vin1-supply = <&pm6125_s6>;
 		pinctrl-names = "default";
 		pinctrl-0 = <&cam_pmic_en_default>;
 
